      {
        "id": 238698,
        "name": "",
        "username": "Thunderbird",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-06-24T01:54:22.555Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, I did kind of the opposite here. Never flipped him, cause I can’t stand the DR and healing. Wipe out Ongoings ASAP, beat him down to 21 over the course of the first two turns. Luminary plays All According to Plan. Guise has a plan, too (Uh, Yeah, I’m That Guy!). Mysterious Ceremony let me Retcon the Master of the Temple before the Dragon could even come out. Luminary gets out a couple Sabre Battle Drones (double boosted). Lay the beatdown on IL, both drones smack him, second blows up the first, Luminary and Guise both react with toxic damage. He went down at the end of Luminary’s third turn IIRC. Mint, 15/16/17.</p>\n<p>Yeah, it was rather an easy Iron Legacy fight. Think it was due to starting with just the cards needed to negate his setup.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-06-24T01:54:22.555Z",
