      {
        "id": 238710,
        "name": "“Mad Dog”",
        "username": "_Mad_Dog",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/_mad_dog/{size}/4859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-06-24T19:20:27.359Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"28623\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don’t even remember what I did, but this was one of the easiest Iron Legacy fights I have ever been in.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Strong agreement, TakeWalker.  I won on Luminary’s turn on round 3.  Things were going so well that I was <em>sure</em> I was overlooking something that was gonna bite me at the end, but it really was that straight-forward.</p>\n<p>Guise was a surprisingly significant character in this fight.  On the end of round 2 Guise had Iron Legacy down to 3 hit points and with “Guise the Barbarian” in play, he only needed a card that would do one. point. of. damage.  Alas, he did not have such a card, so Legacy lived to round 3 and flipped.  Luminary won the day with a “Triple Cross” (a card I don’t use that often).  Iron Legacy was down to 5 hit points when Luminary played this card, and I wasn’t sure it would really work in this case.  It did.</p>",
